{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"IMPORTANT: The Lit adapter is currently experimental and v0.1. Pin exact versions if you need extra release stability while the API is early."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install Lit Query with Lit and TanStack Query Core:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"bun add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query-core"},{"type":"text","value":" is a peer dependency of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-query"},{"type":"text","value":". Even though the Lit docs import user-facing APIs from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-query"},{"type":"text","value":", your app should install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query-core"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"requirements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirements"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit Query is intended for Lit 2.8 and newer, including Lit 3. It uses Lit reactive controllers and Lit context, so query consumers should be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactiveControllerHost"},{"type":"text","value":" instances such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitElement"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query is optimized for modern browsers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Chrome >= 91\nFirefox >= 90\nEdge >= 91\nSafari >= 15\niOS >= 15\nOpera >= 77","lang":"txt"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":", provide it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientProvider"},{"type":"text","value":", and register your custom element. The package exports the provider class but does not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"customElements.define"},{"type":"text","value":" for you."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"subclass-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subclass Pattern"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass AppQueryProvider extends QueryClientProvider {\n  constructor() {\n    super()\n    this.client = queryClient\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('app-query-provider', AppQueryProvider)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<app-query-provider>\n  <todos-view></todos-view>\n</app-query-provider>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"direct-provider-element","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct Provider Element"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can register the provider class directly and bind its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client"},{"type":"text","value":" property from a Lit template. The dot is important: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".client=${queryClient}"},{"type":"text","value":" is a property binding, not an HTML attribute."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\ncustomElements.define('query-client-provider', QueryClientProvider)\n\nclass AppRoot extends LitElement {\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      <query-client-provider .client=${queryClient}>\n        <todos-view></todos-view>\n      </query-client-provider>\n    `\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a connected provider has no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client"},{"type":"text","value":", it throws. See the generated "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/classes/QueryClientProvider.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full contract."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-roots","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render Roots"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The snippets in these docs use Lit's default shadow DOM. Lit Query controllers and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" work with shadow DOM and light DOM because they use the host lifecycle and Lit context, not global selectors."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some runnable examples override "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRenderRoot()"},{"type":"text","value":" and return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" so their demo markup stays in light DOM for shared page styles and test selectors. That override is not required for Lit Query. Use light DOM only when your app has a separate reason to expose a component's internal markup to global CSS, tests, or non-shadow-DOM integration code."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"devtools-status","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Devtools Status"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit Devtools are not available yet. This is a current adapter limitation, not an installation step."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"requirements","text":"Requirements","level":2},{"id":"provider-setup","text":"Provider Setup","level":2},{"id":"subclass-pattern","text":"Subclass Pattern","level":3},{"id":"direct-provider-element","text":"Direct Provider Element","level":3},{"id":"render-roots","text":"Render Roots","level":2},{"id":"devtools-status","text":"Devtools Status","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> IMPORTANT: The Lit adapter is currently experimental and v0.1. Pin exact versions if you need extra release stability while the API is early.\n\nInstall Lit Query with Lit and TanStack Query Core:\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\n`@tanstack/query-core` is a peer dependency of `@tanstack/lit-query`. Even though the Lit docs import user-facing APIs from `@tanstack/lit-query`, your app should install `@tanstack/query-core` explicitly.\n\n## Requirements\n\nLit Query is intended for Lit 2.8 and newer, including Lit 3. It uses Lit reactive controllers and Lit context, so query consumers should be `ReactiveControllerHost` instances such as `LitElement`.\n\nTanStack Query is optimized for modern browsers:\n\n```txt\nChrome >= 91\nFirefox >= 90\nEdge >= 91\nSafari >= 15\niOS >= 15\nOpera >= 77\n```\n\n## Provider Setup\n\nCreate a `QueryClient`, provide it with `QueryClientProvider`, and register your custom element. The package exports the provider class but does not call `customElements.define` for you.\n\n### Subclass Pattern\n\n```ts\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass AppQueryProvider extends QueryClientProvider {\n  constructor() {\n    super()\n    this.client = queryClient\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('app-query-provider', AppQueryProvider)\n```\n\n```html\n<app-query-provider>\n  <todos-view></todos-view>\n</app-query-provider>\n```\n\n### Direct Provider Element\n\nYou can register the provider class directly and bind its `client` property from a Lit template. The dot is important: `.client=${queryClient}` is a property binding, not an HTML attribute.\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\ncustomElements.define('query-client-provider', QueryClientProvider)\n\nclass AppRoot extends LitElement {\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      <query-client-provider .client=${queryClient}>\n        <todos-view></todos-view>\n      </query-client-provider>\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf a connected provider has no `client`, it throws. See the generated [`QueryClientProvider` reference](./reference/classes/QueryClientProvider.md) for the full contract.\n\n## Render Roots\n\nThe snippets in these docs use Lit's default shadow DOM. Lit Query controllers and `QueryClientProvider` work with shadow DOM and light DOM because they use the host lifecycle and Lit context, not global selectors.\n\nSome runnable examples override `createRenderRoot()` and return `this` so their demo markup stays in light DOM for shared page styles and test selectors. That override is not required for Lit Query. Use light DOM only when your app has a separate reason to expose a component's internal markup to global CSS, tests, or non-shadow-DOM integration code.\n\n## Devtools Status\n\nLit Devtools are not available yet. This is a current adapter limitation, not an installation step.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: installation\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\n> IMPORTANT: The Lit adapter is currently experimental and v0.1. Pin exact versions if you need extra release stability while the API is early.\n\nInstall Lit Query with Lit and TanStack Query Core:\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add @tanstack/lit-query @tanstack/query-core lit\n```\n\n`@tanstack/query-core` is a peer dependency of `@tanstack/lit-query`. Even though the Lit docs import user-facing APIs from `@tanstack/lit-query`, your app should install `@tanstack/query-core` explicitly.\n\n## Requirements\n\nLit Query is intended for Lit 2.8 and newer, including Lit 3. It uses Lit reactive controllers and Lit context, so query consumers should be `ReactiveControllerHost` instances such as `LitElement`.\n\nTanStack Query is optimized for modern browsers:\n\n```txt\nChrome >= 91\nFirefox >= 90\nEdge >= 91\nSafari >= 15\niOS >= 15\nOpera >= 77\n```\n\n## Provider Setup\n\nCreate a `QueryClient`, provide it with `QueryClientProvider`, and register your custom element. The package exports the provider class but does not call `customElements.define` for you.\n\n### Subclass Pattern\n\n```ts\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass AppQueryProvider extends QueryClientProvider {\n  constructor() {\n    super()\n    this.client = queryClient\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('app-query-provider', AppQueryProvider)\n```\n\n```html\n<app-query-provider>\n  <todos-view></todos-view>\n</app-query-provider>\n```\n\n### Direct Provider Element\n\nYou can register the provider class directly and bind its `client` property from a Lit template. The dot is important: `.client=${queryClient}` is a property binding, not an HTML attribute.\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\ncustomElements.define('query-client-provider', QueryClientProvider)\n\nclass AppRoot extends LitElement {\n  render() {\n    return html`\n      <query-client-provider .client=${queryClient}>\n        <todos-view></todos-view>\n      </query-client-provider>\n    `\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf a connected provider has no `client`, it throws. See the generated [`QueryClientProvider` reference](./reference/classes/QueryClientProvider.md) for the full contract.\n\n## Render Roots\n\nThe snippets in these docs use Lit's default shadow DOM. Lit Query controllers and `QueryClientProvider` work with shadow DOM and light DOM because they use the host lifecycle and Lit context, not global selectors.\n\nSome runnable examples override `createRenderRoot()` and return `this` so their demo markup stays in light DOM for shared page styles and test selectors. That override is not required for Lit Query. Use light DOM only when your app has a separate reason to expose a component's internal markup to global CSS, tests, or non-shadow-DOM integration code.\n\n## Devtools Status\n\nLit Devtools are not available yet. This is a current adapter limitation, not an installation step.\n"}
